{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Big Argument"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Getting Over It"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use these tenses  to express that an action began in the past and is still going on or has just finished. The past action is <span class=\"strong\">connected to the present</span> in some way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "To talk about a <span class=\"strong\">result</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">recently completed action</span>, use the <span class=\"underline\">Present Perfect tense</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Regular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + base form of verb + <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Irregular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + past participle of irregular verbs"}, {"type": "text", "content": " To talk about the duration of an action, use the <span class=\"underline\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Continuous</span> is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + <span class=\"italic\">been</span> + base form of verb + <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: It feels like <span class=\"strong\">you've been thinking</span> a lot about Camilla lately."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: Of course I have! In fact, <span class=\"strong\">I've been trying</span> to get in touch with her recently. <span class=\"strong\">I've been</span> so unlucky with my dates lately. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Showing You Understand Someone's Feelings or Situation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Showing <span class=\"strong\">empathy</span> is an important part of natural conversation. It means that you understand someone else's situation. It makes the other person more comfortable talking to you, which can extend the conversation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to show <span class=\"strong\">empathy</span>, use expressions like: <br> <span class=\"italic\">It sounds like ... </span><br> <span class=\"italic\">It feels like ... <br/> <br/></span> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">It sounds like the two of you were confused.<br/>It feels like you've been thinking a lot about this.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It feels like you could learn a lot from him."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It sounds like you've been having a hard time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It feels like you have more to say about the subject."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It seems like I could do more to help you."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to have a crush"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be infatuated with someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally told me that Camilla has a crush on me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about an emotional situation."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "obvious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "predictable and easily understood"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I only found out she had a crush on me after Sally pointed out that it was pretty obvious."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "anxious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "nervous"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I just feel anxious whenever I know I have to call someone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pointer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "advice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Mike has been giving me pointers on how to be more relaxed on a date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nerd"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone obsessively interested in a particular subject "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm a comic book nerd. Not all my dates understand that."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get over"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to recover from an upsetting experience"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've been unlucky with my relationships lately. Maybe I should just get over the whole dating thing ... "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le01ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Identify some of the most common problems people have when dating."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Have a partner do the same and then read one of your problems to your partner, then have  them read one to you."}, {"type":